# GitHub issue labels

When creating issues with `gh issue create`, always pass `--label`. Fetch the current set with `gh label list` if unsure. Do not create unlabeled issues.

For a defect, use `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/bug_report.md` as the body (description, reproduce steps, expected vs actual, environment). Do not open a public issue for a vulnerability or a conduct report.

Pick labels from this repo. Combine when more than one applies (for example `architecture` + `testing`).

| Label | Use when |
| --- | --- |
| `bug` | Something is broken or behaves incorrectly |
| `enhancement` | New feature, improvement, or product gap |
| `architecture` | Design, structure, protocols, or split/refactor decisions |
| `testing` | Missing tests, coverage, or verification |
| `documentation` | Docs, comments, or clarifying how something works |
| `question` | Needs a decision or more information before work |
| `good first issue` | Small, well-scoped, suitable for a newcomer |
| `help wanted` | Extra attention is needed |

Do not use `duplicate`, `invalid`, or `wontfix` on new issues unless that is the explicit conclusion.

Example:

```bash
gh issue create --title "..." --label "bug" --body "..."
gh issue create --title "..." --label "architecture" --label "testing" --body "..."
```
